Do not share type trees between the expansions of a quote

A quote is unpickled once and cached, and each later use copies the cached
tree so that its definitions are unique. The copy keeps the nodes it has no
reason to change, among them every type tree whose type names nothing
defined in the quote. So the expansions of a macro in one compilation unit
share those type trees.

Capture checking records the type it makes for a type tree against the node,
with capture sets and root capabilities that belong to the definition the
tree is part of. A shared node therefore gives the second expansion what was
made for the first, which is out of its scope:

    Note that capability `any²` cannot flow into capture set {any}
    because any² is not visible from any in an enclosing function.

for the parameter of a closure made for a context function argument, and

    because postable$proxy2 in method second is not visible from any in
    value request.

for the ascription of an anonymous class instance. The copy of a cached
quote now has a type tree node of its own for each occurrence.

Found in Soundness's obligatory (two expansions of telekinesis's `submit`)
and in exegesis and espionage (several of obligatory's `JsonRpc.serve`).
The first case reproduces on stock scala/scala3 3.10.1 and 3.10.2-RC2.

